---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test catch without parens\nWRITE RAISE \"x\" CATCH e => \"caught\"\n\n; Catch with success (no error)\nWRITE 42 CATCH e => 0\n\n; Catch division by zero\nWRITE (1 // 0) CATCH e => -1\n\n; Pattern match on error type (Raise)\nWRITE RAISE \"error msg\" CATCH e => {\n  MATCH e {\n    Error.Raise(msg) => { \"raised: {msg}\" }\n    Error.Runtime(msg) => { \"runtime: {msg}\" }\n    _ => { \"other\" }\n  }\n}\n\n; Division by zero is Runtime; must return Int to match\nWRITE (1 // 0) CATCH e => {\n  MATCH e {\n    Error.Runtime(msg) => { -1 }\n    _ => { -2 }\n  }\n}\n\n; String expression with Runtime error match\nWRITE \"{\"test\"}{RAISE \"oops\"}\" CATCH e => {\n  MATCH e {\n    Error.Raise(msg) => { \"caught raise: {msg}\" }\n    _ => { \"other error\" }\n  }\n}\n"
---
"caught"
42
-1
"raised: error msg"
-1
"caught raise: oops"
